      "message": "So we are effectively restoring what was originally implemented in 6.12: https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/kernel/common/+/3702536 where we had:\n```\nstatic void *admit_host_page(void *arg)\n{\n\tstruct pkvm_memcache *host_mc \u003d arg;\n\n\tif (!host_mc-\u003enr_pages)\n\t\treturn NULL;\n\n\tif (__pkvm_host_donate_hyp(host_mc-\u003ehead, PAGE_SIZE)) {\n\t\tWARN_ON(1);\n\t\treturn NULL;\n\t}\n\n\treturn pop_pkvm_memcache(host_mc, hyp_phys_to_virt);\n}\n\n/* Refill our local memcache by popping pages from the one provided by the host. */\nstatic int refill_memcache(struct pkvm_memcache *mc, unsigned long min_pages,\n\t\t    struct pkvm_memcache *host_mc)\n{\n\tstruct pkvm_memcache tmp \u003d *host_mc;\n\tint ret;\n\n\tret \u003d  __topup_pkvm_memcache(mc, min_pages, admit_host_page,\n\t\t\t\t     hyp_virt_to_phys, \u0026tmp);\n\t*host_mc \u003d tmp;\n\n\treturn ret;\n}\n```\n@dmaluka@google.com, do you maybe recall why it was changed during porting to 6.18 in https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/kernel/common/+/3941664?",
